# =============================================================================
# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE EVIDENCE IN THIS REPOSITORY
# =============================================================================
#
# core.autocrlf=true was set on the machine this project was built on, and
# there was no .gitattributes. The consequence was found on 2026-09-03 by
# cloning the repository and hashing what came out:
#
#     PHASE6_HOLDOUT_FREEZE.txt  in this working tree   b36befd3...248f6
#     PHASE6_HOLDOUT_FREEZE.txt  in a fresh clone       8373973b...
#
# A clone converted every LF to CRLF on checkout, so on any second machine the
# freeze failed its own sha256, frozen_manifest.py --verify failed on every
# text file, the freeze validator's V1a failed, and phase6_score_holdout.py
# REFUSED TO RUN because its S0a assertion did not match.
#
# THE FREEZE'S ENTIRE EVIDENTIAL VALUE IS ITS HASH. A hash that only holds in
# one working tree is not evidence, and pushing the repository did not make it
# portable - it made a second copy that disagreed with the first.
#
# So conversion is turned off for everything whose bytes are hashed, and the
# artefacts pandas writes with CRLF on Windows - which is what the manifest
# recorded - are pinned to CRLF explicitly rather than left to depend on each
# machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# DO NOT REMOVE THESE RULES. Verify a change to them by cloning and hashing,
# not by reading the diff: the diff is exactly what does not show it.
# =============================================================================

# Frozen documents, code and the report - byte-for-byte, no conversion.
*.txt   -text
*.md    -text
*.py    -text

# Audit and result artefacts, and the two frozen JSON specs. Written CRLF on
# Windows and hashed that way in FROZEN_MANIFEST.txt, so they are checked out
# CRLF everywhere rather than depending on each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# The first version of this file had *.json as -text and a clone came back
# with two MOVED hashes. Verified by cloning, not by reading.
*.csv   text eol=crlf
*.json  text eol=crlf

# Sources.
*.xls   binary

# These two as well.
.gitattributes -text
.gitignore -text
